# Pairs with CausalOrder. A lost in-flight batch moves the acknowledged cursor past it instead of
# rewinding the drain, so the watermark vouches for entries the receiver never saw.
MODULE: CausalOrderLossCountedAsDelivered
TARGET: CausalOrder
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a transport loss is acknowledged as delivered, so S passes the lost entries
PERTURBS: LoseA
BOUNDS: Parts = {1}, MaxLoss = 1

--- FIND
    /\ adr' = [adr EXCEPT ![p] = aack[p]]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: the loss is acknowledged.
    /\ aack' = [aack EXCEPT ![p] = adr[p]]
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED Origin /\ UNCHANGED <<aack, bdeps, back>> /\ UNCHANGED Rcv
--- REPLACE
    /\ UNCHANGED Origin /\ UNCHANGED <<adr, bdeps, back>> /\ UNCHANGED Rcv
--- END
